title dexter line editor -- the bounded input line, the terminal's input half, GREEN
prompt autonomous loop -- read REMEMBER + the three road-ahead docs, take the next agent-doable lap Lindy-first crux-first, send often, stop at custody gates
think Read the road ahead: REMEMBER (living edge scooter_view r3 at 77b799400c), the 1024-round itinerary, the eight-season double-seat (Season G, the terminal family), and the Rye-first crypto/decision-wave doc. The Dexter/Scooter plan names round 5 next: the line editor.
think Lindy-first crux-first: scooter_view r3 gave Dexter its OUTPUT half (a channel's journal folded into a bounded 24x80 frame). The card and the drawn-frame design each name the INPUT half -- a live TTY with a cursor -- as Dexter's own later rung. The bounded editable line is the crux beneath it: pure arithmetic over a byte buffer, reused by every prompt the terminal family will ever draw, ungated, finishable green in one lap. The wire between Constel piers stays the serve gate (the maintainer's hand).
think Built pond/apps/dexter_line.rye: a Line of at most 256 bytes with a cursor, insert (printable ASCII only, shifting the tail right), backspace and delete_forward (shifting the tail left), move_left/right/home/end, and clear. Every operation keeps cursor <= len <= max_line by construction; before/after split the line at the cursor for a prompt to draw. Named errors: LineFull, NonPrintable, CursorAtStart, CursorAtEnd -- refused by name, never a silent no-op.
obs GREEN on the first metal run. tame_style_check first flagged the selftest's `) == error.` call-seam checks (assert(l.move_right() == error.X)); bound each refused call to a const first (past_end, past_start, overflow, tab, newline, del) matching the scooter_channel house pattern, then bans clean, width-check exit 0. New prose plain ASCII, American spelling.
obs Additive by construction -- a fresh module beside scooter_view; nothing of the channel, keyed, or view rungs was touched. Held pure: no raw terminal, no escape codes, no network -- the editable line is the floor the live-TTY rung stands on.
obs Rota lap (d27, item 22) read context/SILO_TECHNIQUE.md -- receive an idea, understand it, set it down in your own vocabulary with the outside names left in the gratitude room. The ncurses/Ghostty/Dill line-editor lessons enter Dexter siloed; the elders are thanked in the plan's gratitude line, never quoted in the code.
loom witness=dexter_line_witness selftest=GREEN max_line=256 selftest_cases=6
